{{- /*
repo-root.tmpl — the ONLY template-time definition of the repository root, for
a template-time expression that reaches OUTSIDE the deployed tree (a
fingerprint glob against `system/`, `packages/`, `crates/`, `firmware/`, or
`mise.toml`; a bare `glob` call; a deployed command source that bakes a path
at render time).

Input: the source directory string (e.g. `.chezmoi.sourceDir`), not a dict --
there is nothing else to configure.

  {{ $repoRoot := includeTemplate "repo-root.tmpl" $sourceDir }}

Rule, read from chezmoi's own source-root resolution: the source directory's
PARENT when that parent holds a `.chezmoiroot` file, else the source
directory itself. That makes this partial's return value the source directory
today (no `.chezmoiroot` exists yet) and `dir .chezmoi.sourceDir` once a later
unit adds one at the repository root -- with no edit to this file in between,
because the file only ever reads the marker, never assumes its presence.

A source-relative expression (one that stays inside the deployed tree, such as
a `.chezmoidata/*.yaml` or `dot_local/...` glob) keeps resolving through
`.chezmoi.sourceDir` directly and MUST NOT call this partial -- only a
cross-root expression does.
*/ -}}
{{- $sourceDir := . -}}
{{- $parent := dir $sourceDir -}}
{{- if stat (joinPath $parent ".chezmoiroot") -}}
{{- $parent -}}
{{- else -}}
{{- $sourceDir -}}
{{- end -}}
